{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/382577-is-blessed-is-the-god-king-really-overpowered-for-deceived","id":382577,"title":"Is blessed is the god-king really overpowered for deceived?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-26T18:48:46-08:00","id":382577,"title":"Is blessed is the god-king really overpowered for deceived?","content":"Seriously...the power to summon a god onto your essence, even at sekhem 1, which can then blaze to sekhem 10, regenerate pillars and willpower like crazy, and then learn utterances it doesn't know. That sounds kinda scary, I am sure many arisen groups had a very short descent after running into one of those things. Oh...and it is free","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T18:56:24-08:00","id":382593,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the most significant thing about the power seems to be that it renders the user Incorporeal, thus scuppering any attempt to fight back unless the opponent has one of a few very specific powers that allows them to interact with incorporeal beings (such as Words of Dead Hunger and Ancestry of Forgotten Stars).<br /> <br /> Other than that, it's not anymore egregious than regular Blessed Is The God-King cast by a Mummy with two or more Pillars at 5.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure it actually needed to be free, but I don't feel that it being so renders it overpowered.<br /> <br /> That all said, I believe it's an Epic Unleashing. In a white room scenario, yeah, it's pretty powerful. Its fundamental flaw lies in it broadcasting the user's position to everyone with an ounce of mystical power within a not-insignificant-radius. For a species that wants to remain hidden, that's a pretty significant downside. My own players haven't dared use it yet, purely because of the risk of being tracked afterwards. Especially since, in the aftermath, the user has no Willpower or Pillars at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T18:59:45-08:00","id":382600,"title":"","content":"True, it seems like something to use as a last resort. However, it is one hell of a nuclear option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T19:06:34-08:00","id":382604,"title":"","content":"It's undeniably an exceptionally powerful option.<br /> <br /> That said, it's not used lightly and has a raft of mitigating factors that means most players will not be relying upon it. You won't be seeing players waltzing through combats dropping the Utterance at the slightest sign of danger. I'm of the personal belief that its strength as compared to that of other Utterances is a bit immaterial once you take into account how much of a last resort it is.<br /> <br /> In using this Utterance, a Deceived reveals who they are. Against a Mummy with a relatively intact Memory, it's possible they may recognise the figure that appears as one of the Shan'iatu. That's a huge amount of information to volunteer to the target, especially when the figure will almost certainly return from death within a short time period with memory of what it faced intact. In the interests of short-term self-preservation, you're surrendering the massive long term advantage that the Deceived rely upon. Namely, that their existence is considered a myth by the vastly more numerous Arisen.<br /> <br /> I don't think I can stress how much of a bad idea that could be. Many Deceived, to my view, would be more willing to die than risk that Unleashing in front of someone who might recognise the Temakh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}